The population figures inside data/v0.1-2026-05-15 and data/v0.2-ppp-2026-05-15
(spec.json, SOURCES.md) are United Nations World Population Prospects 2024
figures (Copyright (c) 2024 by United Nations, CC BY 3.0 IGO) as republished by
Worldometer (worldometers.info), which both spec.json files and v0.1's
SOURCES.md name as the intermediary; 23 of the 25 values equal the UN file and
two (Greece, Slovenia) differ by one person. Those vintages are superseded by
v0.3 and v0.4, which read the UN file directly; their files are kept unchanged
so that their hashes stay verifiable. The United Nations does not endorse
Worldyard (formerly openunit).

Euro foreign exchange reference rates in every vintage are reproduced from the
European Central Bank (source cited in each vintage's SOURCES.md), which
publishes them for information purposes only; the conversion to US-dollar
cross rates, usd_per_unit(C) = (USD per EUR) / (C per EUR), is a modification
made by Worldyard (formerly openunit). It is stated in the SOURCES.md and
spec.json of v0.1, v0.3 and v0.4; v0.2's nominal-FX baseline applies the same
conversion to the same 2026-05-15 rates as v0.1's valuation leg.
